        "contentEn": "There are six members in a family, named A, B, C, D, E, and F. B is the son of C but C is not the mother of B. A and C are a married couple. E is the brother of C, D is the daughter of A. F is the brother of B.\n\n(A) There are only three male members in the family\n\n(B) A has only three children\n\n(C) A and D are both females\n\n(D) D is a female but A is not a female\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below\n\n1. (A), (B), (C), and (D) are all incorrect\n\n2. (A), (B), (C), and (D) are all correct\n\n3. (A) and (C) are correct but (B) and (D) are incorrect"
